{"id": "EUVD-2026-15238", "enisaUuid": "8f9c637d-5398-3fd7-b9c4-7e3ad24ac1f4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: annotate data-races around sk->sk_{data_ready,write_space}\n\nskmsg (and probably other layers) are changing these pointers\nwhile other cpus might read them concurrently.\n\nAdd corresponding READ_ONCE()/WRITE_ONCE() annotations\nfor UDP, TCP and AF_UNIX.", "datePublished": "2026-03-25T10:26:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:13:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/279f2b67d1c44ee139bd3fdb221850daa9358449", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ad01905831c815520f1b0486336a03bb7420465", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c494448bb522bbbb63096540eb2319101a0480ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f17c1c4acbe2bd702abce73a847a04a196fab2c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/27fccdbcbbfc4651b6f66756e6fa3f52e051ec23", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2ef2b20cf4e04ac8a6ba68493f8780776ff84300"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-23302"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.09, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02267d14-6245-39db-b987-6614c4641ec3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.7"}, {"id": "08134beb-f8fe-3148-ab6e-f402f475f343", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.20"}, {"id": "33dddcb3-a869-31b5-86e4-78fc0570746d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.17"}, {"id": "4693325c-51d0-3ad4-b931-f3215fed3e58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "604326b41a6fb9b4a78b6179335decee0365cd8c <7ad01905831c815520f1b0486336a03bb7420465"}, {"id": "469d5d15-f811-3e54-99bd-3b4742d92216", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5936db49-5d4b-3c68-aca4-14e5de2c91a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.82"}, {"